CVPR-2024-P0192,CVPR-2024-A001011,Jiayi Zhu,shared,3,6,6,"East China Normal University, China New York University, USA IHPC & CFAR, Agency for Science, Technology and Research, Singapore Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Shanghai Industrial Control Safety Innovation Tech. Co., Ltd, China Detection Results Co-salient Object Detectors Detection Results Concept-guided Purification Group Images Containing some Adv. Examples Purified Group Images c Concept Learning CosalPure T2I Diffusion Learned concept Validation of c Figure . Examples of our method C OSAL P URE and comparative results before and after purification. C OSAL P URE comprises two modules: group-image concept learning and concept-guided purification. Firstly, the concept learning module inputs a group of images that contain some adversarial cases and obtain their shared co-salient semantic information (i.e., the learned concept), denoted as c. We can validate the effectiveness of the learned c through the visualization via a text-to-image (T2I) diffusion model. Secondly, steered by the previously learned concept, we employ certain diffusion generation techniques to purify the entire group of images. Before our purification, the co-salient object detection results are poor, but after purification, the detection results are satisfactory. Please enlarge to see more details.",-5,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P0192.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Zhu_CosalPure_Learning_Concept_from_Group_Images_for_Robust_Co-Saliency_Detection_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
