CVPR-2024-P0239,CVPR-2024-A001258,Hong-Xing Yu,shared,3,11,11,"Girl in wonderland … Stanford University Flamingos … Mad hatter … Google Research Tea party … Chessboard … Red queen … More Examples Serene lake … Cyberpunk city … Input (text or image) Generated wonderjourneys (rendering of generated sequences of 3D scenes) Figure . We propose WonderJourney—generating a sequence of diverse yet coherent 3D scenes from a text description or an arbitrary image such as photos or generated art (“from anywhere”). WonderJourney can generate various journeys (which we refer to as “wonderjourneys”) for a fixed input, potentially ending “everywhere” (Fig. ). We show rendered images along the generated sequence of 3D scenes. We strongly encourage the reader to see video examples at",0,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P0239.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Yu_WonderJourney_Going_from_Anywhere_to_Everywhere_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
