CVPR-2024-P0386,CVPR-2024-A002082,Tan Wang,shared,3,9,9,"Nanyang Technological University Microsoft University at Buffalo Skywork AI Advanced Micro Devices Generated Image/Video (Baselines vs. Ours) Unseen Reference FG & BG MRAA Unseen Target Pose T2I DisCo DreamPose Adaptor (a) Generalizability (b) Compositionality Target Pose (from source B) DisCo Reference FG (from source A) Reference BG (from source C/D/E/F) Generated Image/Video (Ours) Figure . We propose D IS C O for human dance generation on social media platforms, focusing on two key properties compared to conventional human motion transfer: (a) Generalizability: generalizable to unseen human subject (FG), background (BG) and pose; (b) Compositionality: adapting to the arbitrary composition of FG, BG and pose, each from a different source.",-18,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P0386.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Wang_DisCo_Disentangled_Control_for_Realistic_Human_Dance_Generation_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
