CVPR-2024-P1059,CVPR-2024-A005871,Razvan-George Pasca,shared,3,8,8,"NVIDIA KU Leuven INSAIT, Sofia Future TransFusion Estimated position of next active object Past observable frames Multimodal fusion model Prediction frame verb noun TTC stir pan .52s Input egocentric video Object detector, spoon; hold pan Image captioner, ... Models for context extraction Estimated next action + time to contact Language context Figure . TransFusion: Multimodal fusion transformer for short-term object interaction anticipation. Given a video sequence of past observations, the task aims to predict a set of objects visible in the current frame that will be interacted with in the future, i.e. in the activation frame that is ∆ frames away from the current prediction frame. Additionally, the task requires estimating the bounding box, the associated action described by a verb-noun pair, and the time to contact for each predicted object. We propose TransFusion, a multimodal fusion architecture that uses language summaries of past actions and salient objects to effectively predict future object interactions.",-6,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P1059.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Pasca_Summarize_the_Past_to_Predict_the_Future_Natural_Language_Descriptions_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
