CVPR-2024-P1193,CVPR-2024-A006667,Zizhang Li,shared,3,9,9,"Stanford University UT Austin University of Oxford kyleleey.github.io/3DFauna/ Figure . Learning Diverse 3D Animals from the Internet. Our method, 3D-Fauna, learns a pan-category deformable 3D model of more than different animal species using only 2D Internet images as training data. At test time, the model can turn a single image of an quadruped instance into an articulated, textured 3D mesh in a feed-forward manner, ready for animation and rendering.",-4,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P1193.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Li_Learning_the_3D_Fauna_of_the_Web_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
