CVPR-2024-P1222,CVPR-2024-A006857,Jiazhi Yang,shared,3,14,14,"OpenDriveLab and Shanghai AI Lab Hong Kong University of Science and Technology University of Hong Kong University of Tübingen Tübingen AI Center OpenDV-2K GenAD + hours Multimodal Driving Data Generalized Predictive Model t YouTube Driving Videos Tasks t+ . Zero-Shot Generalization Observed t+ … Diverse Paired “ Texts ” KITTI GenAD … “ Forward ” Public Driving Datasets VLM / LLM Imagined Waymo Cityscapes Iterative & joint denoising . Language-conditioned Prediction . Action-conditioned Prediction Control with different texts (command/context) Control with different future trajectory Imagine . Planning Control with highlevel command Imagine “Turn left towards the mountain” GenAD “Change to the left lane” Lightweight Planner Predicted Trajectory Figure . Overview of the GenAD paradigm. We aim to establish a generalized video prediction paradigm for autonomous driving by presenting the largest multimodal driving video dataset to date, OpenDV-2K, and a generative model that predicts the future given past visual and textual input, GenAD. The strong generalization and controllability of GenAD is validated spanning a diverse spectrum of tasks, including zero-shot domain transfer, language-conditioned prediction, action-conditioned prediction, and motion planning.",-3,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P1222.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Yang_Generalized_Predictive_Model_for_Autonomous_Driving_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
