CVPR-2024-P1231,CVPR-2024-A006904,Shengbang Tong,shared,3,6,6,"FAIR, Meta Q: Is the door of the truck cab open? No, the door of the truck is not open in the image provided. Q: Is the edge of the heart in the picture white or dark-colored? The image you've provided is small and of low resolution, but it appears that the hearts have a dark-colored edge or outline. This outline varies in visibility, likely due to the quality of the image. UC Berkeley Q: In this image, how many eyes can you see on the animal? The image shows one eye of the animal. It's a close-up of a bald eagle facing slightly to its right, which presents only one side of its face to the viewer. Q: Is the school bus parked facing the camera or away from the camera? The school bus is parked facing away from the camera. You can tell because the rear lights and the back of the exterior rearview mirror are visible. The text ""SCHOOL BUS"" is also reversed, which is typically seen on the front of a bus, designed so that it reads correctly in a rearview mirror. Q: How many wheels can you see in the image? In the image provided, I can see two wheels on the visible side of the car. Q: Are the butterfly’s feet visible? The butterfly's feet are not visible in this image. The wings and part of the body of the butterfly are in view, but the feet are either hidden beneath the body or out of the frame of the picture. Butterflies have delicate, slender feet which are often not the most noticeable feature when they are perched, especially from the angle shown in this image. Figure . Instances are systematically identified where the visual question answering (VQA) capabilities of GPT-4V [",-7,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P1231.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Tong_Eyes_Wide_Shut_Exploring_the_Visual_Shortcomings_of_Multimodal_LLMs_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
