CVPR-2024-P1239,CVPR-2024-A006948,Rui Li,shared,3,6,6,"Technical University of Munich . Introduction Humans have the extraordinary ability to estimate the geometry of a 3D scene from a single image, often including its occluded parts. It enables us to reason about where dynamic actors in the scene might move, and how to best navigate ourselves to avoid a collision. Hence, estimating the 3D scene geometry from a single input view is a long-standing challenge in computer vision, fundamental to autonomous navigation [",-2,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P1239.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Li_Know_Your_Neighbors_Improving_Single-View_Reconstruction_via_Spatial_Vision-Language_Reasoning_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
