CVPR-2024-P1813,CVPR-2024-A010180,Tsai-Shien Chen,shared,3,11,11,"Snap Inc. University of California, Merced University of Trento HDVILA-100M Panda-70M (Ours) “Yeah, now everybody thought that we couldn't replace cat; yeah, because you're such animal lovers.” “It is a close-up shot of a brown and white english bulldog with wrinkles on its face, sitting on a person's lap.” “It's good that we have aquariums they bring this wonderful experience into our homes for special moments” “It is a red and purple betta fish swimming in a tank with gravel and plants.” “We're gonna cook this all together stirring it constantly for just a minute until it smells nice and fragrant.” “A person is adding chicken broth to a pot of quinoa on a stove.” “He thought he was gonna get shows terrible communication on the teams part.” “A basketball player is dribbling the ball and shooting it into the hoop.” Figure . Comparison of Panda-70M to the existing large-scale video-language datasets. We introduce Panda-70M, a large-scale video dataset with captions that are annotated by multiple cross-modality vision-language models. Compared to text annotations in existing dataset [",-19,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P1813.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Chen_Panda-70M_Captioning_70M_Videos_with_Multiple_Cross-Modality_Teachers_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
