CVPR-2024-P2039,CVPR-2024-A011439,Keyang Zhou,shared,3,4,4,"University of Tübingen, Germany Max Planck Institute for Informatics, Saarland Informatics Campus, Germany InterCap GRAB ObMan Figure . We propose GEARS, a method to synthesize sequence of hand poses during interaction with an object. GEARS takes hand and object trajectory as input. It generates realistic hand poses that are well-adapted to object surface, irrespective of object category and size. We show sample results on different datasets. Hands colored in blue are inputs while hands colored in cyan are our predictions.",0,data/raw/cvpr/2024/first_pages/CVPR-2024-P2039.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/papers/Zhou_GEARS_Local_Geometry-aware_Hand-object_Interaction_Synthesis_CVPR_2024_paper.pdf
